  "note": "Samshaptakas are warriors who have taken an oath and these warriors (primarily the Trigartas) take an oath to die or kill Arjuna. This sec-tion is named after that oath. With Arjuna out of the way, the idea is that Drona will capture Yudhishthira. On the twelfth day of the battle, Arjuna kills several of the samshaptaka warriors. Drona kills many of the Panchalas, Matsyas and Kekayas. Bhima kills the king of Anga. Bhagadatta kills the king of Dasharna and Ruchiparva and unleashes the vaishnava weapon on Arjuna, which is countered by Krishna. Arju-na kills Bhagadatta. Arjuna kills Vrishaka and Achala, Shakuni�s brothers. Ashvatthama kills Nila of Mahishmati. Arjuna kills three of Kar-na�s brothers. CHAPTER 993(16)",
